concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3 Definitions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-3 ;
    values:originalText "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears: ACT Branch means the branch of the Australian Public Service referred to in subsection 21(2) of the A.C.T. Self-Government (Consequential Provisions) Act 1988. ACT officer means a person who is an officer within the meaning of the Public Sector Management Act 1994 of the Australian Capital Territory. Public Service Act means the Public Service Act 1922. transfer day means the day on which this Act commences." ;
    skos:definition "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears: ACT Branch means the branch of the Australian Public Service referred to in subsection 21(2) of the A.C.T. Self-Government (Consequential Provisions) Act 1988. ACT officer means a person who is an officer within the meaning of the Public Sector Management Act 1994 of the Australian Capital Territory. Public Service Act means the Public Service Act 1922. transfer day means the day on which this Act commences."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "42db720883d6292c5db663d25e6bd352e8be29222eb4145ac4d316fd7d0041a0" ;
